Chapter: RealApproxNegate

 Plugs 1.45's second half. `real-mode-compare` builds its negative operands
 with `0.0 - x`, which is a SUBTRACTION, so nothing in it reaches the negate
 emitter and it passes on every lane while negate is wrong. This calls
 `negate` on a `Real approximate` and prints what comes back.

 The riscv emitter is the one measured wrong: it moved the value with
 `fmv.d.x` and flipped the sign with `fsgnjn.d`, which is bit 63, where an
 f32's sign is bit 31 -- so the value came back unchanged and, having had bit
 63 set, unboxed as well.

Section: Operands

  ran-pos : Real
  ran-pos = 2.5

  ran-small : Real
  ran-small = 1.5

Section: The Path

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  approx-neg : Real approximate -> Real approximate
  approx-neg (a) = negate a

  approx-lt : Real approximate, Real approximate -> Integer
  approx-lt (a) (b) = b2i (a < b)

 A negate that does nothing leaves the value positive, so this answers 0
 where it should answer 1. A negate that unboxes leaves the next f32
 operation reading NaN, and a comparison against NaN is False, so that
 answers 0 too. The two failures are indistinguishable here on purpose:
 either way the row is wrong, and the row below separates them.

  approx-round-trip : Real approximate -> Integer
  approx-round-trip (a) = b2i (negate (negate a) < a)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("neg pos is negative   want 1: " & integer-to-text (approx-lt (approx-neg (to-real-approx ran-pos)) (to-real-approx 0.0)))
    print-line-uni ("neg 2.5 lt neg 1.5    want 1: " & integer-to-text (approx-lt (approx-neg (to-real-approx ran-pos)) (approx-neg (to-real-approx ran-small))))
    print-line-uni ("double negate not lt  want 0: " & integer-to-text (approx-round-trip (to-real-approx ran-pos)))
    print-line-uni ("neg neg is positive   want 0: " & integer-to-text (approx-lt (approx-neg (approx-neg (to-real-approx ran-pos))) (to-real-approx 0.0)))
  end
